{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_spec_reviews_2026_09_23_judge_project_mgmt", "label": "Karvey 3.11.1 Review: Project-Management Judge (PM)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/spec/reviews/2026-09-23-judge-project-mgmt.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Strong traceability and quality control, weak work management: artifacts exist but nobody aggregates or measures them."}, {"id": "docs_spec_reviews_2026_09_23_judge_project_mgmt_pm_01", "label": "PM-01: Single phase state machine with a validator that detects lies", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/spec/reviews/2026-09-23-judge-project-mgmt.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A board is useful only if its state is true; even the author cannot keep it by hand."}, {"id": "docs_spec_reviews_2026_09_23_judge_project_mgmt_pm_02", "label": "PM-02: Do not overwrite the estimate with actual time; store both and measure accuracy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/spec/reviews/2026-09-23-judge-project-mgmt.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An estimate never compared with the outcome is an opinion; the code erases the evidence."}, {"id": "docs_spec_reviews_2026_09_23_judge_project_mgmt_pm_03", "label": "PM-03: 'deployed' must mean in production, not PR open (deploying state)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/spec/reviews/2026-09-23-judge-project-mgmt.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deployed vs released distinction is what the client cares about."}, {"id": "docs_spec_reviews_2026_09_23_judge_project_mgmt_pm_04", "label": "PM-04: Release manifest: dev->master PR ships everything in dev", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/spec/reviews/2026-09-23-judge-project-mgmt.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Approval must cover exactly what is released; approved unit (change) != released unit (branch)."}, {"id": "docs_spec_reviews_2026_09_23_judge_project_mgmt_pm_05", "label": "PM-05: Flow and DORA metrics from existing data (phase_history)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/spec/reviews/2026-09-23-judge-project-mgmt.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Without measuring approval wait time, the 'human review is the bottleneck' claim is untestable."}, {"id": "docs_spec_reviews_2026_09_23_judge_project_mgmt_pm_06", "label": "PM-06: Complete karvey-context dashboard with aging and WIP limits", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/spec/reviews/2026-09-23-judge-project-mgmt.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "WIP limits and aged-work visibility are Kanban basics; invisible work stays 'almost done'."}, {"id": "docs_spec_reviews_2026_09_23_judge_project_mgmt_pm_07", "label": "PM-07: Stakeholder visibility: periodic report and 'your turn' events", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/spec/reviews/2026-09-23-judge-project-mgmt.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "In a consultancy the client reads neither spec.json nor the internal channel."}, {"id": "docs_spec_reviews_2026_09_23_judge_project_mgmt_pm_08", "label": "PM-08: Cost per change (tokens, USD) also with a single agent, per client", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/spec/reviews/2026-09-23-judge-project-mgmt.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Per-client margin depends on knowing the cost per delivery."}, {"id": "docs_spec_reviews_2026_09_23_judge_project_mgmt_pm_09", "label": "PM-09: Scale ritual cost to work size (batching, small lane, attributed -y)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/spec/reviews/2026-09-23-judge-project-mgmt.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Too-expensive rituals end up skipped; Kanban classes of service formalize proportionality."}, {"id": "docs_spec_reviews_2026_09_23_judge_project_mgmt_pm_10", "label": "PM-10: Unambiguous WBS: 'Feature' means two things", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/spec/reviews/2026-09-23-judge-project-mgmt.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A WBS must be a single scope decomposition (PMI 100% rule)."}, {"id": "docs_spec_reviews_2026_09_23_judge_project_mgmt_pm_11", "label": "PM-11: Pending decisions (Q-NN) and risks with owner and deadline", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/spec/reviews/2026-09-23-judge-project-mgmt.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Decision/risk logs without owner and date are files, not management tools."}, {"id": "docs_spec_reviews_2026_09_23_judge_project_mgmt_pm_12", "label": "PM-12: Retro that measures method output, is saved and feeds the backlog", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/spec/reviews/2026-09-23-judge-project-mgmt.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A retro without process data or action follow-up is the costliest ceremony per return."}, {"id": "docs_spec_reviews_2026_09_23_judge_project_mgmt_pm_13", "label": "PM-13: Global sequential IDs collide across parallel work", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/spec/reviews/2026-09-23-judge-project-mgmt.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Traceability depends on unique identifiers."}, {"id": "docs_spec_reviews_2026_09_23_judge_project_mgmt_pm_14", "label": "PM-14: Multi-client, multi-project portfolio view", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/spec/reviews/2026-09-23-judge-project-mgmt.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Portfolio management is central for a multi-tenant consultancy."}, {"id": "docs_spec_reviews_2026_09_23_judge_project_mgmt_pm_15", "label": "PM-15: Backlog with prioritization criteria (WSJF) and full lifecycle", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/spec/reviews/2026-09-23-judge-project-mgmt.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Economic prioritization turns a list into a plan."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_spec_reviews_2026_09_23_judge_project_mgmt", "target": "docs_spec_reviews_2026_09_23_judge_project_mgmt_pm_01", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/spec/reviews/2026-09-23-judge-project-mgmt.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_spec_reviews_2026_09_23_judge_project_mgmt_pm_01", "target": "plugins_karvey_skills_karvey_skill", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/spec/reviews/2026-09-23-judge-project-mgmt.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_spec_reviews_2026_09_23_judge_project_mgmt_pm_01", "target": "plugins_karvey_skills_karvey_requirements_skill", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/spec/reviews/2026-09-23-judge-project-mgmt.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_spec_reviews_2026_09_23_judge_project_mgmt_pm_01", "target":